Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00
; ============================================================================
; Download Manager Companion — Native Messaging host registration (EXAMPLE)
; *** NOT TESTED ON WINDOWS HERE ***
; This VM has no Windows machine, so these steps are a template for the
; desktop-app installer / a user on Windows to adapt and verify. Do NOT
; assume they work untested: verify on a real Windows + Chrome/Edge/Brave
; install before shipping, and prefer having the desktop installer write
; these keys itself (with the real install path and extension ID).
;
; What this does:
;   Tells Chrome (HKCU key below) where to find the host manifest JSON.
;   The browser then launches the host executable named in that JSON's
;   "path" field whenever the extension calls chrome.runtime.connectNative
;   with the matching host name. No other app can impersonate the extension:
;   the JSON's allowed_origins must contain the extension's real ID.
;
; Before importing:
;   1. Replace REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_EXTENSION_ID in
;      com.downloadmanager.nextgen.json with the real ID from
;      chrome://extensions (Developer mode -> the unpacked extension's ID,
;      or the Web Store ID once published).
;   2. Replace C:\Program Files\DownloadManagerNextGen\... in that JSON
;      with the real installed host executable path.
;   3. Copy that JSON to the SAME path used in the registry value below
;      (or edit the value to point at the JSON's real location).
;   4. Double-click this .reg file (or merge it with regedit) as the
;      CURRENT user (HKCU — no admin rights needed for this key).
; ============================================================================

; --- Google Chrome ---
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Google\Chrome\NativeMessagingHosts\com.downloadmanager.nextgen]
@="C:\\Program Files\\DownloadManagerNextGen\\com.downloadmanager.nextgen.json"

; --- Microsoft Edge (uncomment if Edge support is required) ---
; [HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Edge\NativeMessagingHosts\com.downloadmanager.nextgen]
; @="C:\\Program Files\\DownloadManagerNextGen\\com.downloadmanager.nextgen.json"

; --- Brave (uncomment if Brave support is required) ---
; [HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\BraveSoftware\Brave\NativeMessagingHosts\com.downloadmanager.nextgen]
; @="C:\\Program Files\\DownloadManagerNextGen\\com.downloadmanager.nextgen.json"

; --- To UNINSTALL (remove registration only; delete the JSON/exe separately) ---
; Delete the keys above, e.g. in regedit:
;   HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Google\Chrome\NativeMessagingHosts\com.downloadmanager.nextgen
; Or save the following as uninstall.reg and merge it:
; Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00
; [-HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Google\Chrome\NativeMessagingHosts\com.downloadmanager.nextgen]
